  "body": "Stacked on #1139 (on #1123, #560, #551). fork synced at v0.19.0.\n\nExpected merges: retarget to `main` after #1139 merges. #1143 (Wire UI, also on #1139) touches `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wire_page.rs`; this PR changes one line there (the op destructure gains `..`), so a trivial conflict at most. #534 (verify) and #1109 (open profile) on #1123 are not touched.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe Wire Contour gains skim passes: a rough pass, then N skims, each naming its own machine condition (and so its own offset, wire radius + that condition's gap), with an optional direction reversal per skim.\n\n- `operation::WireContourOp.skims: Vec<WireSkim { condition, reverse }>`; file / MCP JSON `skims: [{ condition, reverse? }]`, absent when empty (rough-only files and goldens unchanged). Edits ride `EditOperationParams` (undoable) and the existing MCP params door.\n- Command door (`wire_op::condition_of`): every skim's condition resolved through #531's door, refused by name when it names none or the machine does not state it; then `motion::wire_edm::check_passes`: a pass nearer the profile than the finishing (last) pass (\"would cut past the finished profile\", rough included), a skim farther out than the pass before it (\"would cut only air\"), a skim condition with another wire diameter (\"one threading cuts every pass with one wire\").\n- Generator: `motion::wire_edm::wire_passes` (new `skims.rs`) runs #532's single-pass generator per pass at its own offset, every law at that offset; each pass leads in from the threading point and back; a reversed skim walks clockwise. No skims is `wire_contour` exactly.\n- Stamp digests each skim's condition numbers and direction (writes nothing for no skims - no stored stamp moves).\n- Post stream (`posting_wire`): a mid-section `PARAM EdmCondition <skim id>` before each skim's first move (after each return to the threading point); a path that does not return once per pass is refused.\n- `wire-iso.cps`: a condition that arrives with the wire threaded is the next skim's - `(SKIM n)`, the condition select and `comp_off` again at its first move; the wire stays threaded.\n- **Wire laws (#534) and skims** (merge with main, 2026-11-13): `sim::verify::wire` now judges each move at its own pass's kerf. Before this, every move was judged at the rough's kerf, which read skim 1 as a false 0.0200 mm gouge at move 8 (0.165 - 0.145). `WireJob.skim_offsets`, new `passes.rs`: the path is split at each return to the threading point, the threading law takes the widest pass, and the slug law sweeps each pass at its own offset. Skims on an open run are refused at the door and in the law. The arithmetic is in the decision record.\n- **Sodick wire post refuses skims** (second merge-time refresh, main after #1506): `assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps` writes its C condition word once, at threading, so a skim's mid-section `PARAM EdmCondition` would only have reassigned a variable and every skim would have been cut on the rough pass's condition. A condition change after the section's first cut is now refused by name: \"Sodick: a condition change between passes (skims) is not supported by this post - post the skims through wire-iso or as separate operations\". No C word is written per pass (no public Sodick source for a mid-program condition change, #617). `wire-iso.cps` is the only other shipped wire post and already selects per pass, so it is unchanged. Main's `sodick_wire_post.rs` literal gains `skims`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/538-wire-skims.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/wire-iso/wire_contour_punch_skims.nc` (rough C110 + skim S21 + reversed skim S31 on #533's synthetic fixture): three distinct offsets (X-20.165 / -20.145 / -20.135), three condition selects, one thread, one cut.\n- `wire_post`: `a_rough_and_two_skims_post_three_offsets_and_condition_selects`, `no_skims_is_the_rough_program_and_json_unchanged`, `skims_edit_undo_and_round_trip`, `each_skim_refusal_is_named_at_the_door`; the existing `the_punch_contour_posts_its_golden_through_the_gate` passes with #533's golden unchanged (no golden moved).\n- `camcraft-motion` unit: `skims_cut_their_own_offsets_and_none_is_the_single_pass`, `skim_laws_refuse_by_name`.\n- `camcraft-sim` unit: `verify::wire::tests::each_pass_is_judged_at_its_own_kerf`, `passes_that_cannot_be_told_apart_are_unreadable`.\n- `wire_contour` suite (all 7) green; `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/533-wire-iso-post` on head 0e96ca1c: motion, app (every suite - the new golden is shared input) and ui suites, 0 failed (12.4 min). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n- `sodick_wire_post::skims_are_refused_by_name_never_cut_on_the_rough_condition`: a rough C110 + skims C121, C131 through `post_script` is refused by name with no file, and through the engine neither skim C word is written. **Mutation check:** with the refusal block removed from `sodick-wire.cps` the test is RED (the skimmed program posted, `expect_err` panicked); restored, GREEN. Sodick goldens and `wire_contour_punch_skims.nc` unchanged.\n- Second refresh, head 7d8a125a: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` post, sim, motion, app, ui suites 0 failed (31.8 min), the four pinning tests included; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-{geometry,cl,tools,post,sim,motion,app,ui} --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real EDM control (D10): the fixture's conditions and codes are synthetic (three synthetic conditions S21, S31, W20 added to it).\n- A punch drops after its rough unless held - tabs are #539; the program does not claim a hold.\n- No UI editor for the skim list yet: follow-up #1148 (after #535 / #1143).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Wire Contour skim passes - a rough pass then N skims, each at its own machine condition's offset (optionally reversed), posted by the generic ISO wire post with a condition select per pass; out-of-order or unstated skims refused by name (#538)\n\nFixes #538\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
